## 6. Open Problems

1. **The Wick angle rate dθ/dt.** Underdetermined. Candidates: 1/t_P (Planck rate), 1/(kL·t_P) (warp rate), 1/(J·t_P) (coupling rate). The framework does not fix the natural time unit.

2. **The nine perturbation values.** Stored, not derived. An origin in a deeper structure (e.g., a covering group, a larger database, a different assignment of modes to particles) has not been found.

3. **The shape parameters r.** Stored, not derived. The shape parameter is a property of the full mode vector (64 components), but the framework does not specify how it is computed.

4. **Why four references?** The reference entries cover all four charge categories. Whether this is structural (four is the dimension of the charge space) or coincidental is open.

5. **The crossover ratio base 0.8653.** The crossover ratios follow a base-0.8653 exponential. Close to 5/6 and to 1 − 1/(H/2). Not exact.

6. **Flavor physics.** CKM and PMNS matrices are open. If the processor picture applies, they would be additional stored entries in a flavor-sector database.

7. **The cosmological mapping.** The 7/32 residual is derived. Whether this maps quantitatively to the observed cosmological constant is open.

